From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phoenix new GPU lane <noreply@phoenix-rtos.invalid>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] meson: no dril_dri shared stub on Phoenix-RTOS

The X11 platform (or GLX=dri) always builds gallium/targets/dril: the
<driver>_dri.so stub an X server's AIGLX loads with dlopen(). Phoenix-RTOS
builds Mesa static-only (patch 0002: the gallium megadriver is an archive
linked into every program) and has no dynamic linker to load the stub, so the
shared_library() link fails (libphoenix is not PIC). Skip the target there;
EGL on X11 (DRI3) does not use it.
---
 src/meson.build | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -161,7 +161,11 @@
   subdir('egl')
 endif
 if with_gallium
-  if with_glx == 'dri' or with_platform_x11
+  # dril_dri is the shared-object stub an X server's AIGLX dlopen()s as
+  # <driver>_dri.so; a static-only system (Phoenix-RTOS: no dynamic linker,
+  # the gallium megadriver is linked into every program) cannot build it and
+  # has no loader for it.
+  if (with_glx == 'dri' or with_platform_x11) and host_machine.system() != 'phoenix'
     subdir('gallium/targets/dril')
   endif
 endif
